### Page 1 of 2

```text
ORDINANCE NO. ____________________

ENTITLED: “AN
ORDINANCE
AMENDING
THE
CHEYENNE
UNIFIED
DEVELOPMENT CODE (UDC), AS APPROVED BY ORDINANCE NO.
3943 ON JANUARY 23, 2012, TO ADDRESS ISSUES RAISED
REGARDING CITY SIGN REGULATIONS.”

BE IT ORDAINED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE,
WYOMING:

Section 1. That on December 5, 2011, the Cheyenne Planning Commission unanimously
recommended approval of the “Cheyenne Unified Development Code”.

Section 2. That on January 23, 2012, the Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne
unanimously approved the Unified Development Code (Ordinance No. 3943) with an effective
date of April 30, 2012.

Section 3. That on February 19, 2013, the City of Cheyenne Planning Commission held a
public hearing to satisfy the Unified Development Code Annual Review Requirement (ref. UDC
1.1.7).

Section 4. That on October 21, 2013, the Cheyenne Planning Commission recommended
approval of certain amendments related to City sign regulations similar to those herein.

Section 5.  That the section “Temporary Signs”, in Table 6-14, Sign Types, be amended
to read, “Any sign which is easily placed and removed from the ground or building without
needing additional structures, construction or specialized equipment.”

Section 6.  That the section “Temporary Signs” in Table 6-15, Residential District Sign
Allowances, is deleted and hereby changed to the following bullets, inclusive:
• Other than Neighborhood/District Identification Signs, parcels located in residential
zoning districts shall not contain signs having an aggregate sign area greater than thirty-
six (36) square feet.
• No individual sign shall exceed twelve (12) square feet in sign area in a residential
zoning district.

Section 7.  That the section “Temporary Signs” in Table 6-15, Non-Residential District Sign
Allowances, is deleted and hereby changed to include the following bullet, inclusive:

• No individual sign shall exceed thirty-six (36) square feet in sign area in a non-
residential zoning district.
```

### Page 2 of 2

```text
Section 8.That a sentence be added as UDC Section 6.5.4(b)2.(h) to read “Temporary signs
bearing a message that promotes a business or attempts to generate good will for a business,
or any message that advertises a product or service for sale, or any message that proposes a
commercial transaction shall be limited to two per site. Any applicant that requests an
increase in signage for an event taking place over a finite period of time shall request and be
granted a permit for not more than two (2) periods of consecutive time, neither period to
exceed twenty days in length, per calendar year, which will allow unlimited signage on the
premises of said event.”

Section 9.  That various sentences in Section UDC Section 6.5.5(b), be amended to read as
follows:

“2. The changing of advertising copy or message on a painted or printed sign specifically
designed for the use of replaceable copy.”

“4. Temporary signs. The prohibition on additional structures, construction, or specialized
equipment applies to any lighting that may be considered.”

“5. Nonilluminated incidental signs in residential districts relating to the safety and function
of the site.”

“7. Deleted in its entirety.”

“8. Traffic safety signs and other public safety symbols.”

“12. Deleted in its entirety.”

Section 10.  That this ordinance shall be in full force and effect upon its approval and
publication.

FIRST READING:

SECOND READING:

THIRD AND FINAL READING:

RICHARD L. KAYSEN, MAYOR
(SEAL)
ATTEST:

___________________________________
CAROL INTLEKOFER, CITY CLERK

publish date:  ________________________
```
